12
00:38:40,000 --> 00:38:46,000
Storks is a 2016 American animated adventure comedy film directed by
Nicholas Stoller and Doug Sweetland, and written by Stoller.

13
00:41:53,333 --> 00:41:59,333
The film features the voices of Andy Samberg, Kelsey Grammer, Katie Crown,
Keegan-Michael Key, Jordan Peele, Jennifer Aniston, Ty Burrell, and Danny Trejo.

14
00:45:06,666 --> 00:45:12,666
The film follows two distribution centre employees—hotshot package delivering stork Junior and his
human colleague Tulip—who accidentally create a baby using a defunct baby factory.

15
00:48:20,000 --> 00:48:26,000
In order to protect the baby from the company's manager, the two
embark on a journey to deliver the baby to her family.

16
00:51:33,333 --> 00:51:39,333
The project was announced by Warner Animation Group in January 2013, with
Sweetland attached to direct, and Stoller hired to write the screenplay.

17
00:54:46,666 --> 00:54:52,666
It was announced in April 2015 that Stoller and Sweetland would co-direct the
film, and Stoller would produce the film alongside Brad Lewis.

18
00:58:00,000 --> 00:58:06,000
The main cast was announced soon after.

19
01:01:13,333 --> 01:01:19,333
Mychael and Jeff Danna composed the film's musical score.

20
01:04:26,666 --> 01:04:32,666
The animation was provided by Sony Pictures Imageworks.

21
01:07:40,000 --> 01:07:46,000
Storks premiered at the Regency Village Theater in Los Angeles, California on September 17,
2016, and was theatrically released in the United States by Warner Bros.

22
01:10:53,333 --> 01:10:59,333
Pictures on September 23.

23
01:14:06,666 --> 01:14:12,666
The film received mixed reviews from critics, who praised the
animation, humor and voice acting, but criticized the story.

24
01:17:20,000 --> 01:17:26,000
It was a commercial success, earning $183 million against a $70 million budget.

25
01:20:33,333 --> 01:20:39,333
The film explores themes of baby, villain, stork, delivery service.

26
01:23:46,666 --> 01:23:52,666
The tone is lighthearted.
